-- title:
--   Completeness of reduction on Riemann–Roch spaces, full level
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), and write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field under coefficientwise extension of scalars, and let $\bar F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by the series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $F$ onto $\bar F$ relative to $A$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers} \subseteq F$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $\bar F$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$ on constants, together with a degree-preserving map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places satisfying the divisor pushforward law. Assume $R_0$ is pinned to $q$-expansions: whenever $y \in A((q))$ has image in $F$ under coefficientwise inclusion, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $P_0$ be a place of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and let $n$ be a natural number with $2\,\mathrm{genusFF}(\overline{\mathbb Q}, F) \le n + 1$. Then for every $g \in \bar F$ lying in the Riemann–Roch space of the divisor $n \cdot (R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}\,P_0)$, that is with $v$-adic valuation at most $\exp$ of the divisor value at every place $v$ of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$, there exists $f \in F$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, lying in the Riemann–Roch space of the divisor $n \cdot P_0$, with $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f) = g$.
--
--   This is Deuring's completeness of the reduced linear system for a constant reduction with good behaviour: for $n \ge 2g - 1$ the reduction map carries the integral elements of $L(nP_0)$ onto $L(n\,r(P_0))$, here for the reduction of the full level-$M'$ modular function field at a prime $q \nmid M'$ pinned to $q$-expansions. It is used to produce separating and suitably normalised integral functions on the modular curve, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_cuspRegular_separating`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_cuspRegular_separating) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_rational_integral_cuspRegular_evalAt_ne_of_isRational_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_rational_integral_cuspRegular_evalAt_ne_of_isRational_of_ne).
